uld score 2 points (Prevalent Wind pattern). High cost unless forced.\n\nReason: Both B1 and W7 are completely safe discards due to full exposure. Between them, B1 is part of a pair in my hand, but since all four copies are already visible (my two + next player's three \u2192 total five? Wait: contradiction).\n\nWait \u2014 correction: Each tile has only **four copies**. Next player has [B1,B2,B3] \u2014 that\u2019s one B1. I have two B1s. That leaves only one B1 unaccounted for (possibly discarded or drawn). But in my hand: B1\u00d72, and meld history shows next player played B1 once (in Chi B4 action context?) \u2014 actually, their meld [B1,B2,B3] uses one B1. So total B1s used: 2 (mine) + 1 (meld) = 3. One B1 remains unshown. So **not safe** to assume B1 is dead.\n\nSimilarly, W7: previous player has [W7,W8,W9] \u2014 one W7. I have one W7. Total W7s: 2 used. Two remain unshown. But did anyone else use W7? My history: I played W7 earlier (\"Play W7\"), so I had at least one, now I have one again? Let's check:\n\nMy hand: W7\u00d71  \nMy history: \"Play W7\" \u2014 so I discarded a W7 earlier. That means I held at least one W7 before, and now hold another \u2192 possible only if I drew it back? But you can't draw after discarding same tile unless replacement.\n\nBut each tile only has 4 copies.\n\nLet\u2019s reconstruct W7 usage:\n- Previous player has [W7,W8,W9] \u2192 1 W7\n- I previously played W7 \u2192 1 W7 discarded by me\n- Now I have W7 in hand \u2192 1 W7\n- That\u2019s 3 total. Only one left unshown. So W7 is not fully consumed.\n\nBut wait \u2014 a meld of three tiles uses three copies. No: a chow [W7,W8,W9] uses **one** W7, **one** W8, **one** W9.\n\nSo:\n- [W7,W8,W9] by previous player \u2192 1 W7\n- I discarded W7 earlier \u2192 1 W7\n- I now hold W7 \u2192 1 W7\nTotal: 3 W7s used. One remaining unshown. So **W7 is not safe**.\n\nSame for B1:\n- I have 2 B1s\n- Next player\u2019s [B1,B2,B3] \u2192 1 B1\nTotal: 3 B1s. One unshown \u2192 **not safe**\