ding mine**.\n\nThen:\n- F3:4 \u2192 all 4 F3s are still unshown \u2192 but I have 2, so 2 are in my hand, 2 elsewhere \u2192 possible\n- But then why list F3:4? It's correct if none have been discarded or melded.\n\nCheck discard histories:\n- Did anyone discard F3? My history: Play F2, Play F1, Play F1 \u2014 no F3\n- Next: no F3\n- Across: Play F4, Play F4 \u2014 no F3\n- Previous: Play F2, Play F2 \u2014 no F3\n\nSo no F3 discarded. No meld contains F3. So all 4 F3s are unshown \u2014 yes, possible. I have 2, two are in wall or others' hands.\n\nSimilarly, B1: unshown:2 \u2192 total B1s:4. I have 2, so 2 unshown \u2192 but next player has [B1,B2,B3] \u2192 used one B1 \u2192 so 3 used (2 mine + 1 meld) \u2192 only 1 should be unshown, but listed as 2 \u2192 contradiction.\n\n[B1,B2,B3] uses one B1 \u2192 so total B1s used: 2 (hand) + 1 (meld) = 3 \u2192 one unshown.\n\nBut unshown B1:2 \u2192 conflict.\n\nUnless \u201cunshown\u201d means \u201cavailable in wall\u201d, not in hands.\n\nBut then it should be even smaller.\n\nBest assumption: **\"Unshown tiles\" indicates the number of tiles of that type that are neither discarded nor melded \u2014 i.e., still in the wall or in players\u2019 closed hands (including mine)**.\n\nSo:\n- B1: unshown:2 \u2192 2 B1s not revealed\n- I have 2 B1s \u2192 so both are in my hand \u2192 none in wall or others \u2192 consistent\n- But next player has [B1,B2,B3] \u2014 that requires one B1 \u2192 but if only 2 unshown, and I have 2, then no B1 left for their meld \u2192 impossible.\n\nAh! This is critical.\n\nThe meld [B1,B2,B3] by the next player means they have claimed a B1 from a discard. So one B1 has been revealed (in meld). Therefore, total revealed B1:1.\n\nI have 2 B1s in hand \u2014 these are not revealed to others, but for counting, they exist.\n\nSo total B1s: 4\n- 1 in next player\u2019s meld\n- 2 in my hand\n- 1 must have been discarded or in wall\n\nBut unshown B1:2 \u2192 suggests 2 are still hidden\n\nBut 1 is in